_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.0792,"current":0.1292},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.633,"current":0.844},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.05637209832137069},{"id":"rotation","label":"Consumer Discretionary rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-30,"consecutive_weeks":2,"current":75.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":51.5},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":5.1},{"id":"theme","label":"Travel & Experiences theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"travel-experiences","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":59.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"travel-experiences","theme":"Travel & Experiences","weight":0.5,"order":1,"effective":0.5}],"llm":{"thesis":"Expedia's fundamentals (12% accelerating TTM revenue growth, 123% FCF growth, 72% ROIC, expanding margins) are running well ahead of a valuation still priced near trough multiples (PE at the 3rd percentile of 5-year history, PEG 0.17, FCF yield 13%), producing a 26-point expectations gap. The stock is in a technical uptrend (above 200dma, 50>200 cross, MACD positive) but still 16% off its 52-week high, suggesting the market has not re-rated the business despite clear operating leverage and a fortress balance sheet (net cash position). The main headwind is macro: a Stagflation regime with only moderate Consumer Discretionary sector rotation (36) and a middling Travel & Experiences theme trend (54) caps multiple expansion even as company-level execution improves. This is a quality-compounder-at-a-discount setup that needs either a regime shift (lower inflation/stronger growth) or continued fundamental delivery to close the gap.","fundamental_read":"Revenue growth is accelerating (+12.0% TTM vs +10.0% prior quarter) alongside material operating leverage, with operating margin up 603bps YoY to 16% and FCF margin at 28.4% on 123% FCF growth. ROIC of 72.2% and ROE of 168% reflect a capital-light, high-return model, and the balance sheet is net-cash (net debt/EBITDA -0.49) while shares outstanding are shrinking 5.4% YoY via buybacks exceeding dividends. The only caution flag is that ROIC's trajectory (incremental ROIC) isn't observable, so it's unclear if returns are still expanding at the margin or simply remaining elevated.","technical_read":"Price is in a confirmed uptrend (above 200dma, 50dma>200dma, MACD histogram positive) with neutral momentum (RSI 52.5, near SMA20/50 convergence), consolidating after a 30% 12-month advance and still 15.7% below its 52-week high. The setup looks like a controlled pullback/basing pattern within an uptrend rather than a breakdown, with SMA50 (286.18) acting as near-term resistance/support around the current close (285.93).","market_expectation":"Valuation multiples (PE at 3rd percentile, EV/Sales at 53rd percentile of 5-year history, PEG 0.17) and only moderate capital rotation into Consumer Discretionary (36) imply the market is pricing stagnant-to-modest growth and is not extrapolating the current margin and FCF acceleration into forward estimates \u2014 consistent with a stagflation-era discount on consumer-facing cyclicals.","what_market_misses":["Reality score (69) significantly exceeds pricing score (43), a 26-point gap that historically closes via re-rating if growth persists.","Revenue growth is accelerating, not just high, while the multiple sits near 5-year lows on a P/E basis.","FCF conversion (219%) and margin expansion are compounding faster than the valuation reflects, and buybacks are shrinking the share count, amplifying per-share value creation that may not be fully modeled."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly earnings report (~90 days after 2026-08-06 filing) to confirm continued revenue acceleration and margin trend","Any improvement in Consumer Discretionary sector rotation score from current +36 toward top-decile levels","A shift away from the current Stagflation regime (34.2% probability) toward Reflation or Goldilocks, which would likely re-rate travel/discretionary multiples","Continued buyback execution reducing share count and boosting EPS/FCF per share"],"risks":["Stagflation regime (34.2% probability, highest of the four) is a known headwind for discretionary travel demand and typically compresses multiples further","Consumer Discretionary sector rotation (36) lags defensive sectors (Energy 96, Health Care 94, Consumer Staples 89), indicating capital is not strongly favoring this sector currently","Travel & Experiences theme trend of only 54 suggests the narrative tailwind is moderate, not strong, limiting multiple re-rating catalysts","No engine-flagged idiosyncratic risks were identified, so standard execution, consumer spending, and travel-demand cyclicality risks apply generically","ROIC trend (incremental ROIC) is unobservable, leaving open the possibility that current high returns are a peak rather than still-improving"],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 7% (currently 12.0%)","ROIC falls below 54% (currently 72.2%)","Operating margin YoY change falls below -2.0 pts (currently +6.0 pts)","Consumer Discretionary rotation score stays below -30 for two consecutive weeks (currently +36)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55% (currently combined ~51%)","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","Travel & Experiences theme trend drops below 44 (currently 54.0)"],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Performance-marketing/ad platforms (e.g., Google Search/YouTube, Meta) that capture a large share of Expedia's c